 :question/math-academy-id "q-66902" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that ${e}^{-5z}-6=-2,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z}-6 & =-2 \\\\ {e}^{-5z} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{-5z}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -5z & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z=-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz≈-0.277\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-66902/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "10095048-0db6-5b4e-889f-303f07449367"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66902"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-228897/field-1/fea6f541a81b64b6e4958506d78adea051e2b79e9e3686556b767803f1c7e123" :answer/id #uuid "05d2ae20-b1e6-53c2-8203-599899848b86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.792" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-228897/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bef023fa-665d-5288-8b1a-01eadf984860" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-228897/field-1/fea6f541a81b64b6e4958506d78adea051e2b79e9e3686556b767803f1c7e123" :answer-field/choices ["q-228897/field-1/fea6f541a81b64b6e4958506d78adea051e2b79e9e3686556b767803f1c7e123"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-228897" :question/id #uuid "b2ee8216-6d1d-59ed-ad9d-e2de4dc9dea5" :question/math-academy-id "q-228897" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If ${e}^{x}=6,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x} & =6 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{x}) & =ln⁡(6) \\\\ x & =ln⁡(6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈1.792\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-228897/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "765ef63a-e3f0-503b-876d-3b4776b2cafe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-228897"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263077/field-1/861704f6f9a771c02dcec6d2f8af02da2c04b5eba1896ac0453935c6e0d44ccd" :answer/id #uuid "0c9a635b-aaec-5ca8-97fc-9291250a923e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.732" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263077/field-1/ddfeb0ccefc867c2691f60ae1c11584f6ce80e38615fd35abe85d0579ae88742" :answer/id #uuid "3c91e76d-c3a3-54da-ae5d-dc5e9c149d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.197" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263077/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c9c08d88-1e8e-589f-aba6-9061ff1cb5e6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263077/field-1/861704f6f9a771c02dcec6d2f8af02da2c04b5eba1896ac0453935c6e0d44ccd" :answer-field/choices ["q-263077/field-1/861704f6f9a771c02dcec6d2f8af02da2c04b5eba1896ac0453935c6e0d44ccd" "q-263077/field-1/ddfeb0ccefc867c2691f60ae1c11584f6ce80e38615fd35abe85d0579ae88742"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263077" :question/id #uuid "a2647380-b90f-5a94-b8f2-387bb22f6b39" :question/math-academy-id "q-263077" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If ${e}^{3x}=9,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x} & =9 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3x}) & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ 3x & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}ln⁡(9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.732\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-263077/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "765ef63a-e3f0-503b-876d-3b4776b2cafe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263077"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263081/field-1/c87a1f0b3f6133de1791f6bc7a8b9742b189cd596788c91cd87d3684592fbae1" :answer/id #uuid "ed15ff26-098c-539f-b65f-ec0c6ef615d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.222" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263081/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b00f4e8-2a59-5368-91a6-0a4c4194237c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263081/field-1/c87a1f0b3f6133de1791f6bc7a8b9742b189cd596788c91cd87d3684592fbae1" :answer-field/choices ["q-263081/field-1/c87a1f0b3f6133de1791f6bc7a8b9742b189cd596788c91cd87d3684592fbae1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263081" :question/id #uuid "1d52d063-3aaf-5d01-981f-476f12121b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-263081" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If ${e}^{5-y/2}=\\sqrt[5]{7},$ then $y≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5-y/2} & =\\sqrt[5]{7} \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{5-y/2}) & =ln⁡(\\sqrt[5]{7}) \\\\ 5-\\frac{y}{2} & =ln⁡({7}^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7) \\\\ -\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7)-5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}ln⁡(7)+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈9.222\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-263081/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "765ef63a-e3f0-503b-876d-3b4776b2cafe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263081"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-263199/field-1/dcc03bc005e41c18b4917d65b04b8be6358583d1060a1d2127ab8980f76c4dbc" :answer/id #uuid "c530ded5-7a6d-593d-9882-8064e7270cbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.403" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-263199/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5cf168ad-9b88-5205-8c0b-1711ce4d2696" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-263199/field-1/dcc03bc005e41c18b4917d65b04b8be6358583d1060a1d2127ab8980f76c4dbc" :answer-field/choices ["q-263199/field-1/dcc03bc005e41c18b4917d65b04b8be6358583d1060a1d2127ab8980f76c4dbc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-263199" :question/id #uuid "cba7720d-211d-5524-a5d3-66ab503bec17" :question/math-academy-id "q-263199" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $9-{e}^{3-4x}=5,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{e}^{3-4x} & =5 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =5-9 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =-4 \\\\ {e}^{3-4x} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3-4x} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3-4x}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ 3-4x & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -4x & =ln⁡(4)-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{4}ln⁡(4)+\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.403\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-263199/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "10095048-0db6-5b4e-889f-303f07449367"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-263199"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
